{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^##|''^###|equiv|admit-key|normalize-key|validate-profile|six|P0|neg-pow|canonical-compare|float64'\"\\\\?|4.1.2|floor-int' docs/design/yang.preludes.md\"","aggregated_output":"14:- **2026-11-21 (r5 → r6 hybrid architecture & focused profile scope):** Eliminated guest-UAST host-leak workarounds and collapsed fragmented control subsystems into a **three-tier hybrid model** (aligned with Unison, Koka, and OCaml 5): (1) promoted representation-sensitive pure ops (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed IEEE-754 `yin.vm.float`) into `:pure` host primitives backed by `dao.jing.cbor` / `dao.host.*`, eliminating raw-double stack-frame hazards and guest-side $O(n \\log n)$ sorting; (2) unified `yrt.escape`, `yrt.gen`, safepoint interrupt dispatch, and cold error/limit policy traps into one composable guest algebraic-effect layer (`yrt.effect`) over `%capture` with zero Jolt kernel expansion; (3) focused swappable preludes on **Native profiles** (`py`, `js`, `php`, `clj` for existing code in those languages) plus **N → 1 Yin/Clojure profiles** (`yang.python/clojure-core-v1`, future `yang.typescript/clojure-core-v1`), dropping unnecessary off-diagonal N×M symmetry (such as `:yang.clojure/py-v1`).\n24:## 1. Problem statement and repository baseline\n26:### 1.1 Current repository baseline\n48:### 1.2 Three problems to solve together\n50:1. **Host representation leaks in guest UAST:** Bare VM primitives (`+`, `-`, `=`, `get`, `assoc`, `vec`, `kind/str`) delegate directly to host values, leaking JVM vs. Node/CLJS vs. Dart/CLJD vs. Jolt differences (`Float64` boxing, `BigInt` mixing, `NaN`/`-0.0` equality, CLJS joined-keyword collapse `(keyword nil \"a/b\") == (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`, HAMT map/set iteration order, float formatting). Patching around those leaks in guest UAST produces hundreds of lines of slow, fragile code (`admit-key!`, $O(n \\log n)$ `canonical-compare`, raw-double leaf-frame rules).\n56:## 2. Derivation from foundations and non-negotiable invariants\n60:### 2.1 Foundational axioms & three-tier hybrid rationale\n74:### 2.1a Alignment with the tao architecture's second axiom (`yang.tao.md` §2.2)\n84:### 2.2 Non-negotiable invariants\n103:## 3. Three-tier hybrid architecture & prelude layering\n134:### 3.1 Litmus test: Native Host `:pure` vs. Guest `%capture` Effects vs. VM Effects\n138:| **Tier 1: Native Host `:pure` Core** | Host module exports (`:pure`, effects `#{}`) in `data`, `integer`, `float`, `kind` | **All four hold:** (1) one universal mathematical/representational truth across all languages and all 4 hosts; (2) host-representation-sensitive (avoids `Float64`/`BigInt`/keyword/HAMT leaks); (3) total or status-returning without suspending control flow or calling guest closures; (4) hot-path value operation. | Exact big-int math, boxed IEEE-754 float math & formatting, `data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `data/admit-key?`, `kind/namespace`, code-point strings. |\n142:### 3.2 Explicit exclusions from Layer 2a (`yrt.*`)\n156:## 4. Host `:pure` core extensions & Layer 2a (`yrt.*`) specifications\n158:### 4.1 Native host `:pure` core extensions (`data`, `float`, `kind`)\n165:   - **`data/float64? [x]`:** Backed directly by existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?` (`src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc:212`). Distinguishes float64 carriers from exact integers, booleans, and maps on all 4 hosts.\n166:   - **`data/equiv [a b]`:** Portable IEEE-aware, kind-strict value equality (distinct from content-addressing `data/content=`):\n169:     - Persistent vectors/lists, maps (excluding `:cell-ref` handles), and sets: recursive pairwise/entry equality using `data/equiv`.\n171:   - **`data/admit-key? [k]`:** Recursive portable key/element predicate preventing host map/set collapse (`yin/vm/data.cljc:34–36`, `dao.jing.cbor.md:173, 266`). Returns `true` iff `k` (recursively across vectors, maps, and sets) contains only `nil`, booleans, exact integers, strings, and keywords/symbols whose `name` is free of `\"/\"` and not starting with `\":\"` — **an absent namespace is admitted (r8): the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only, so an unqualified `:k` admits**. Returns `false` for any `float64?` (at any nesting depth), ambiguous identifiers, seqs/lists, closures/continuations, or `:cell-ref` handles. **Integer-carrier normalization (r8):** distinct exact-integer carriers (`int64` vs boxed) normalize recursively on insertion AND lookup so equal integers hit the same entry.\n172:   - **`data/canonical-compare [a b]`:** Total, deterministic comparator over admitted keys/elements. **Normative order (r8):** `dao.jing.cbor.md:173`'s unsigned encoded-byte order is the SINGLE ordering rule — including for compound keys, where elements compare by their encoded bytes rather than a separate recursive clause (the r7 recursive-lexicographic wording is withdrawn as it could disagree with encoded bytes for different-length vectors); identical results on all 4 hosts.\n173:   - **`data/canonical-entries [coll]`:** For a map, returns a vector of `[k v]` pairs sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare` on `k`; for a set, returns a vector of elements sorted ascending by `data/canonical-compare`. Eliminates guest-UAST $O(n \\log n)$ sorting for `keys`, `vals`, `seq`, `reduce`, and `str`.\n180:     - Division/floor/power: `floor` (total IEEE double floor), `floor-int` (exact integer for finite `|x| < 2^53`, else `:yin.vm.float/out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz remainder for finite `x >= 0, y > 0`), `floordiv-mod` (returns `[q r]` boxed pair or `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, preserving `-0.0` quotient sign and `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` rounding correction), `fpow-half` (half-power squaring for `py`/`js`/`clj.py`), `fpow-base` (base squaring for `php`, preserving `1.1 ** 6` bit-exact oracle parity — see D7), `neg-pow` (`[x n pow-order]`, returns boxed `float64` or `:yin.vm.float/underflow`), `parts` (`[mantissa exp2]` exact integer pair).\n185:### 4.2 `yang.call` *(existing Layer-2a leaf)*\n189:### 4.3 `yrt.effect` — Unified guest algebraic effects over `%capture`\n224:  2. **Cold numeric/resource policy traps:** Pure host ops (`yin.vm.integer`, `yin.vm.float`, `data/admit-key?`) return values on the hot path and status keywords on the cold path. Thin guest wrappers call `(yrt.effect/perform ctx :math/overflow ...)` / `:math/div-zero` / `:int/bit-limit` / `:int/digit-limit` / `:coll/unsupported-key` only on the cold branch — letting each language install its own policy handler (e.g., Python `OverflowError`/`MemoryError`/`ZeroDivisionError`, JS `Infinity`/`NaN`, PHP int64-to-float demotion, or deterministic test replay).\n231:### 4.4 `yrt.int` — Exact-integer adapters and radix scanners\n242:### 4.5 `yrt.safepoint` *(Track B — deferred)*\n248:## 5. Declarative prelude composition, recipes, and admission\n252:### 5.1 Emission recipe vs. resolved runtime profile\n254:1. **`:yang.prelude/recipe` (host-side compiler recipe that *emits* a runtime module) — the example below is a TRACK B recipe** (a legacy re-architecture recipe for a native prelude; the P0′ recipes for the Clojure-family modules use the standardized fields):\n301:### 5.2 Composition rules and verified-closure admission\n303:`yang.core.prelude` and `yang.core.prelude-admission` enforce six fail-closed checks. **Home rule (DRY-alignment, r7):** the composition checks (`validate-profile`, `admit-profile`, and their six sub-checks) are implemented in **`yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3 → 5 publics, exactly at the bounded-complexity target), keeping `yang.core.prelude` pure UAST/s-expression emission — the emission/admission boundary is the landed batch-1 seam (`1604aabe`), and the C2 lesson (module duplicating prelude's `host-declaration` was the duplication removed) requires one admission authority, not two namespaces sharing the checks:\n305:1. **Verified artifact closure input (`validate-profile`):** Takes `(profile artifact-store registry)`, where `artifact-store` supplies an immutable content-addressed map of published manifests (`manifest-addr -> verified-manifest`) AND their referenced canonical module trees (`tree-addr -> verified-uast`). Verifies that direct root pins match `:yang.prelude/components`, walks the full transitive `:requires` DAG from `:yang.prelude/root-address`, confirms finiteness and acyclicity, and refuses duplicate bindings for the same linker module symbol.\n310:6. **Dual-emitter standardization & Parity Law:** Standardized linked emission applies to the **P0′ Clojure-family modules** (`:trailing-requires []`, `:finalize-c1? true`) — it does NOT retroactively standardize the frozen native preludes (r8: landed `py` ends its module tree with `require yang.call` and has no C1 finalizer there; php likewise; the bundled clojure continuation family is a left fold — the `:mode` field alone cannot freeze these, so each frozen runtime records its bundled shape, linked trailing forms, dependency pins, and C1 side-table identity-or-absence **independently**). Any program compiled under a composed prelude MUST produce identical outcomes in bundled and linked modes across the semantic, stack, and register VMs (and the AST walker once L-b lands).\n314:## 6. Preludes as swappable libraries: the semantics descriptor contract\n316:### 6.1 Focused profile scope: Yin/Clojure DEFAULT + Native legacy track\n325:### 6.2 Core vs. Frontend ownership boundary\n336:### 6.3 Portable `:yang.semantics/descriptor` schema\n468:### 6.4 Validation, lexical hygiene, authority checks, and parameterization\n483:### 6.5 Frontend SPI and provenance integration (`yang.frontend`)\n493:## 7. Case study: `yang.python` with a `clojure.core` prelude (`:yang.python/clojure-core-v1`)\n495:### 7.1 Value representation & semantic mapping\n510:| Equality `==` / `!=` | `1 == 1.0 == True`, structural list/dict | `data/equiv`: `1 == 1` `true`, `1 == 1.0` `false`, `1 == True` `false`, `NaN == NaN` `false`, `0.0 == -0.0` `true`, recursive over persistent collections |\n514:### 7.2 Portable numeric & collection contract (`clj.py` over `:pure` host core + `yrt.effect`)\n522:     (if (data/float64? x) :float :other))\n525:2. **Int × Int:** Delegates directly to `yin.vm.integer` (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `pow`, `true-div`, `compare`), checking `b == 0` beforehand (performing `:math/div-zero`) and passing every result through `yrt.int/check-limit` before indexing `[q r]` pairs or chaining into further ops. **All host-boundary float carriers are boxed (r8):** `integer/to-float-boxed` for promotion, `integer/true-div-boxed` for division quotients, and boxed `float/neg-pow` for negative exponents — no raw host double enters a guest frame on any Clojure-family numeric path. The frozen native ABI (`integer/to-float`, `true-div`) is unchanged for the legacy track. **Boxed comparison (r8, VM-engineer review):** `integer/compare-float-boxed [x-boxed y-boxed]` (and `integer/from-float-boxed`) are added to the integer host-module exports (listed in §7.2's boxed-path usage) — the landed `compare-float`/`from-float` take raw host doubles and are legacy-only; mixed int×float comparisons on the boxed path never unwrap.\n528:   - `+`, `-`, `*`, unary `-`, unary `+`, `/`, `//`, `%`, `**`, and `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` delegate directly to boxed `yin.vm.float` exports (`float/add`, `float/sub`, `float/mul`, `float/neg`, `float/div-checked`, `float/floordiv-mod`, `float/fpow-half`, `float/neg-pow`, `float/compare`) and `integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper).\n531:   - **Key/element admission:** Map/set construction and lookup in both `clj.py` and `clojure.core.impl` call `(data/admit-key? k)` once; on `false`, perform `:coll/unsupported-key` (raising `{:clj.py/error :unsupported-key :key k}` or `ex-info`).\n532:   - **Equality:** `clj.py/eq` delegates directly to **`data/equiv`**; `clj.py/ne` delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n535:### 7.3 Python lowering Hook ABI & `clj.py` adapters\n550:| `:comp/list-append`, `:comp/set-add`, `:comp/dict-set` | `[acc val]`, `[acc val]`, `[acc k v]` | Validates set elements / dict keys via `data/admit-key?`, updates persistent value inside `acc`, returns `nil`. |\n554:### 7.4 Unified trusted `clj` callable bridge, cross-unit admission, and §8.10.7 validation\n569:### 7.5 Two-module portable `clojure.core` contract (`clojure.core.impl` + `clojure.core`)\n574:   - Requires `yang.call`, `clj`, `yrt.int` (zero direct provenance doors; **zero state cells**). Its guest **policy tags** (`:coll/unsupported-key`, `:math/*`, `:int/*`) live in the handler contract installed by the owning entry (`clj.py/run-main` at P3′, plain `yang.clojure`'s own cold-error policy at P2′) — they are NOT part of the linker-derived VM effect footprint; only the underlying **VM effects** its definitions perform are declared through the existing linker footprint mechanism (`yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc`). Host dependencies: `kind` (with `kind/namespace`), `data` (with `float64?`, `equiv`, `admit-key?`, `canonical-compare`, `canonical-entries`), `integer` (`:min-bits 53`), `float`, and `cell` (for cell checks/updates only).\n579:     - `impl-not=`: delegates to `(not (data/equiv a b))`.\n582:     - Map/set mutators and lookups (`impl-assoc`, `impl-get`, `impl-contains?`, `impl-conj`, `impl-disj`, `impl-merge`, `impl-into`, etc.): enforce `data/admit-key?`.\n589:### 7.6 Concrete lowering example\n601:- `%`, `*`, `+`, `==` lower hygienically to `clj.py/mod`, `clj.py/mul`, `clj.py/add`, `clj.py/eq` (backed by `:pure` `yin.vm.integer` / `yin.vm.float` / `data/equiv`).\n607:## 8. Portability, content addressing, and malleability\n609:### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n616:### 8.2 Dependency graph and malleability (`docs/agents/malleability.md`)\n618:Verified with `clj ./bin/analyze-deps.clj` (r7: the analyzer's high-degree predicate now counts combined in+out degree ≥ 6, matching this document's rule; `56d17563`). No multi-node cycles and no multi-node SCCs exist. The analyzer prints three SELF-loop warnings (`yang.php.antlr.quoted`, `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude` — macro self-reference in defquoted-family namespaces); these are analyzer-reporting artifacts, not runtime dependency cycles, and are expected to disappear once the defquoted consolidation (P0) lands:\n622:Layer B (Pure Composition):      yang.core.prelude, yang.core.semantics, yang.core.defquoted (P0 host macro ns)\n634:### 8.3 Content-addressing and golden discipline (Clean-Slate)\n636:Per the Owner Clean-Slate Directive, regenerate affected golden snapshots cleanly per slice (`P0`–`P4`) and validate correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and CPython/Node/PHP language-oracle parity suites.\n640:## 9. Phased implementation roadmap and acceptance gates\n646:| **P0′ — Composition plumbing & `:pure` host core extensions** | Implement `:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`, `validate-profile` + `admit-profile` **in `yang.core.prelude-admission`** (3→5 publics, per the §5.2 home rule); add `:pure` host exports (`data/float64?`, `data/equiv`, `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`, `data/canonical-entries`, `kind/namespace`, and boxed `yin.vm.float` across all 4 hosts); consolidate `defquoted` into `yang.core.defquoted` (dedicated host macro namespace, keeping `yang.core.prelude` at 11 publics — naming per r8 M9, consistent across §8.1/§8.2); base-prelude emitter recipes record the *current* per-prelude modes as migration truth (`:linear` for `py`, `:balanced` for `php`/`js`; the bundled `yang.clojure` continuation family is a LEFT FOLD, not balanced — recorded as its own mode so the freeze is exact) without changing shapes. | No golden churn for py/js/php (no shape change); new modules get fresh addresses | Closure, missing-manifest, `host-limits`, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint tests; 4-host test suite for `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`, `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`, `data/canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries`, and `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 -> :underflow`, `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`); existing py/php oracle suites unchanged-green. |\n648:| **P2′ — Unified `clojure.core` + `yang.clojure` migration** | Publish collision-free `clojure.core.impl` (pure, `impl-*` prefix, `admit-key?`-guarded) + cell-free `clojure.core` facade; migrate `yang.clojure` directly onto unified `clj` + `clojure.core`. | Refresh `yang.clojure` goldens cleanly | Native collection invocation through the new standard library (the locally-bound-map `:k` → 9 fixture) and bundled primitive shadowing of bare `get`/`assoc` (which otherwise resolve through the source store before VM primitives); unified `yang.clojure` suite green. The real `clj → clj.py → clj` cross-syntax unwind (cleanup + context restoration) gates ONLY at P3′, after `clj.py` exists. |\n649:| **P3′ — Descriptor parameterization + `clj.py` + `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (the DEFAULT flip)** | Implement generic `yang.core.semantics` with UAST-derived arity & role validation; define the python frontend contract; refactor `yang.python.antlr.lower` to read literals/hooks/capabilities from `:yang.semantics/descriptor` (the legacy `py-v1` descriptor pins today's `'py/*` hooks 1:1 — behavior-preserving, gated by the existing CPython oracle suites); publish `clj.py`; flip `yang.python`'s default `runtime-profile` to `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` (a revision re-pin in `yang.frontend`). | py goldens regenerate under the descriptor-driven path (legacy descriptor byte-identical outcomes); clojure-core-v1 gets fresh goldens | Legacy-descriptor behavior preservation: full CPython corpus + 4-host parity under `py-v1` pin; end-to-end 4-host `:yang.python/clojure-core-v1` suite (numeric/float ops, `:max-bits 53` limit traps, `data/admit-key?` refusals, `data/equiv`, `data/canonical-entries` ordering, deterministic `str`/`gensym`); the cross-syntax `clj → clj.py → clj` unwind gate — cleanup and context restoration, exactly once per activation — listed directly here; capability refusal tests (typed `except E:`, `genexpr` under `:control/generators :refused`); default-profile regressions (r8): an unqualified `:k` key admits successfully (the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only); equal exact integers in different host carriers hit the same map entry on insert AND lookup; a local/projected value equal to `:clj/unbound` remains distinguishable from an absent binding; canonical traversal order matches Jing encoded-byte order (`0` before `nil`); UAST-derived validation rejecting wrong arity, non-lambda hooks, unqualified hooks, reserved doors, out-of-closure exports. |\n655:## 10. Owner decisions and disposition ledger\n664:3. **D3 — Python float tagging (r7: moot until Track B — py keeps its tagged `{:py/float}` representation as-frozen; boxed `yin.vm.float` ships for the Clojure path in P0′):**\n668:   - Settled in favor of clean golden regeneration per slice (`P0`–`P4`), preserving correctness via behavioral, 4-host, and language-oracle suites rather than frozen-quirk backwards compatibility.\n674:7. **D7 — Float exponentiation rounding (r7: `fpow-half` ships in P0′ for the Clojure path; `fpow-base` defers to Track B with the php re-architecture):**\n675:   - *Option A (Recommended for P0/P1 — Architect concurred):* Export both `float/fpow-half` and `float/fpow-base` in `yin.vm.float` so `1.1 ** 6` preserves bit-exact parity (`0x1.c585058dde7acp+0` for `py`/`js` vs `0x1.c585058dde7abp+0` for `php`) across existing CPython/Node and PHP language oracles.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/yang-base/1795208263748-engineer-yang-preludes-p0prime.prompt.md\ncat collab/yang-base/1795207345010-vmengineer-yang-preludes-r8-review.deepseek-v4-pro.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-11-20 20:57:43 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-11-21 03:57:43 +07 (Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh)\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: yang-preludes-P0prime-implementation\nRole: Engineer\n\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-terra | Assigned: 2026-11-21 03:57:43 +0700 | Status: active | Rationale: continuity with the landed DRY rounds; the P0′ slice is the design's own extension of the seams this family implemented and had reviewed\n\nImplement slice **P0′** of the signed-off design `docs/design/yang.preludes.md` (r8, architect\nSIGN-OFF + VM-engineer SOUND — read it first, especially §4.1, §5.1–5.2, §9 P0′, §8.1–8.2).\nYou may edit files and run tests in this worktree (detached at current origin/master).\n**Do not commit, do not push, do not touch collab/.** Scratch scripts in /tmp. Match\nsurrounding style.\n\n## Deliverables (per the signed-off design; the r7/r8 reviewer conditions are binding)\n\n### 1. `:pure` host core extensions\n- **`yin.vm.data` additions** (`src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc`): `data/float64?` (delegating to\n  the existing `dao.jing.cbor/float64?`), `data/equiv` (portable IEEE-aware kind-strict\n  equality per §4.1.1: exact-int×exact-int via `integer/compare`; float64×float64 IEEE with\n  NaN≠NaN and +0.0==-0.0; exact-int×float64 FALSE; kind-strict keywords/symbols so\n  `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")` on CLJS too; recursive vectors/maps-ignoring-\n  cell-refs/sets; other scalars host `=`), `data/admit-key?` (recursive; **absent namespace\n  ADMITTED — the namespace-non-empty rule applies to two-part keywords only**; name free of\n  \"/\" and not starting with \":\"; refuses float64 at any depth, ambiguous identifiers,\n  seqs/lists, closures, `:cell-ref`), `data/canonical-compare` and `data/canonical-entries`\n  (**normative order: Jing's unsigned encoded-byte order per `dao.jing.cbor.md:173` — `0`\n  before `nil` — as the SINGLE ordering rule, including compound keys compared by encoded\n  bytes; the r7 recursive-lexicographic clause is withdrawn**).\n- **NEW `yin.vm.float`** (`src/cljc/yin/vm/float.cljc`, module name `'float`, all `:pure`,\n  effects `#{}`, ALL 4 HOSTS — JVM/CLJS/CLJD/Jolt per the `yin.vm.integer` v4 pattern):\n  boxed `data/float64` in/out, exports per §4.1.2: constants/predicates (`inf`, `neg-inf`,\n  `nan`, `zero`, `neg-zero`, `nan?`, `finite?`, `zero?`, `neg-zero?`, `zero-like`), IEEE\n  arithmetic (`add`, `sub`, `mul`, `div`/`div-checked` → `:yin.vm.float/div-zero`, `neg`\n  preserving `-0.0`, `abs`, `compare` → `-1/0/1` or `:nan`), `floor`, `floor-int` (exact for\n  |x| < 2^53 else `:out-of-range`), `fmod-pos` (Sterbenz), `floordiv-mod` (`[q r]` or\n  `:div-zero`, `-0.0` quotient sign, `2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0` correction), `fpow-half` (for\n  py/js/clj.py), `neg-pow` (`:underflow`), `parts`, `format` (deterministic 4-host via\n  `dao.host.float/float-digits`; `NaN`/`Infinity`/`-Infinity`/`0.0`/`-0.0`/`1.0 -> \"1.0\"`).\n  **`fpow-base` is DEFERRED to Track B** (D7 r7 note) — php keeps its existing mechanics.\n  **Host-boundary conversion rule:** add `integer/to-float-boxed` and\n  `integer/true-div-boxed` (+ `from-float-boxed`) to `yin.vm.integer` — boxed results only;\n  the legacy `to-float`/`true-div` stay for the frozen native track.\n- **`kind/namespace [x]`** added to the kind module (locate it — design §4.1.3 says\n  `yang.clojure/kind-module`).\n\n### 2. Composition plumbing\n- **`yang.core.defquoted`** (NEW host macro namespace): consolidate the `defquoted`\n  ClojureDart AOT macro from `yang.python.antlr.prelude`, `yang.typescript.antlr.prelude`,\n  and `yang.php.antlr.quoted` — the three namespaces require the new one; their self-loop\n  analyzer warnings should disappear. `yang.core.prelude` stays at 11 publics (the macro\n  does NOT go there — reviewer condition).\n- **`:yang.prelude/recipe` / `:yang.prelude/profile`** schemas (§5.1 exactly) +\n  **`validate-profile`** (verified `:yin.module/tree` closure walk, finiteness/acyclicity,\n  duplicate-binding refusal, direct provenance-door ban on non-trusted modules vs.\n  transitive footprint ceiling via `:yang.prelude/max-effects`) and **`admit-profile`**\n  (host-export admission via the existing `prelude-admission/admit`, `host-limits` floors\n  `:min-bits`/`:min-digits`/`:min-max-items` failing closed) — **implemented in\n  `yang.core.prelude-admission` (3→5 publics, exactly at bound; `yang.core.prelude` stays\n  pure at 11 — reviewer condition)**.\n- **Base-prelude emitter recipes as migration truth:** a recipe record per existing base\n  prelude recording its CURRENT mode (`:linear` for py, `:balanced` for php/js) and C1/\n  trailing-requires facts AS LANDED — recorded, not changed. No existing prelude's UAST\n  shape changes; existing content addresses are FROZEN (zero golden churn for py/js/php).\n\n## Mandatory validation plan\n\n1. **Baseline first:** the existing py/php oracle + parity suites must pass UNCHANGED before\n   your edits (they are the frozen-track regression net). Run: the php + python parity/\n   prelude namespaces you used in the batch-1 round, plus `yang.clojure-test`.\n2. **New-primitive suites (4-host where the lane allows):** `data/equiv` (`[0.0] == [-0.0]`,\n   `[NaN] != [NaN]`, `(keyword nil \"a/b\") != (keyword \"a\" \"b\")`), `data/admit-key?`\n   (unqualified `:k` admits; two-part keyword rules; float refusal at depth),\n   `canonical-compare`/`canonical-entries` (Jing encoded-byte order: `0` before `nil`),\n   `yin.vm.float` (`2.1 // 0.7 == 3.0`, `-0.0 // 2.0 == -0.0`, `0.5 ** -2000 → :underflow`,\n   `format` `1.0 -> \"1.0\"`), `validate-profile`/`admit-profile` (closure, missing-manifest,\n   host-limits, direct-provenance vs. transitive-footprint, duplicate bindings). JVM+Node on\n   this host; **CLJD and Jolt implementations must be WRITTEN (the cljc + host files), with\n   their lane gates noted as follow-up** if the lanes are heavy — the orchestrator routes\n   them.\n3. **Regression net after edits:** the same focused namespaces as baseline + `analyze-deps`\n   (the defquoted self-loops should be GONE; report the count).\n4. `git diff --check` clean.\n\n## Constraints\n\n- No UAST node type, no VM opcode, no manifest schema change, no closed language registry.\n- `yang.core.prelude` stays pure emission (11 publics); admission grows only in\n  `prelude-admission` (3→5).\n- Zero shape/address change to the landed py/js/php preludes and their goldens.\n- The frozen native ABI (`integer/to-float`, `true-div`) is unchanged.\n\n## Report format (mandatory)\n\nBegin exactly:\nCompleted-GMT: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS GMT>\nCompleted-Local: <YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS +07>\n\nThen: deliverable-by-deliverable summary (files, exports, LOC), the baseline-vs-after gate\ntable with counts, the analyzer self-loop count before/after, noticed-but-not-done. End with:\nVERDICT: DONE — <one line> | or | BLOCKED — <why>\nCreated-GMT: (in the report body)\nCreated-Local: (in the report body)\nCoding-Agent: deepseek\nSession-ID: 8e4174e5-ebb7-499a-bca8-60827de40a38\n# Task: yang-preludes-r8-vmengineer-review\nRole: Yin.VM Runtime Engineer\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-11-20 20:47:51 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-11-21 03:47:51 +07\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 risk | §2.1 axiom 4 / §4.3 `handle`-`perform` | Continuation-portability envelope under-specified\n\n`%capture`-based delimited continuations (resumable one-shot `handle`/`perform`, and the Track-B generator driver that \"stores the captured continuation `k` and resumes `(k sent-val)`\") place `k` in the task-local `ctx-cell`. `state.md` states the lift encoder refuses closures/continuations as `:yin.k/non-portable`, and application/invocation refuses a continuation whose owner is not the task's. The design never pins whether `%capture` reifies a portable `yin.vm.values/Continuation` or a host reification, so captured continuations are **task-local and non-serializable**. This is fine for the landed within-task one-shot pattern, but sits in tension with the \"everything is a continuation\" portability narrative and any Track-B generator checkpoint/stream serialization. The `restore!` `:base`-preservation rule is sufficient *within* a task's suspension/resumption, not *across* tasks.\n\n**Correction:** add one sentence pinning the envelope — `%capture` continuations are task-local, non-portable, resumable only within their task — and state explicitly that generator suspension cannot serialize a paused `k` across tasks/streams.\n\n### P1 risk | §7.2 item 3 mixed int×float comparison | `integer/compare-float` is a residual raw-double path\n\n`integer.cljc` v3/v4 `compare-float` takes a **raw host double** (`float!` → `host/host-float?`), as does `from-float`. §7.2 says mixed `<`/`>` delegate to \"`integer/compare-float` (via boxed float helper)\", but §4.1's integer additions list only `to-float-boxed`/`true-div-boxed` — no `compare-float-boxed`. Either `clj.py/lt` unwraps a boxed `data/float64` via `data/float-value` (a raw double transiently on the guest stack, violating invariant 3's zero-raw-double claim on a hot path), or a new boxed export is required but unlisted. Promoting the int to float would round it, so exact int×float comparison cannot substitute.\n\n**Correction:** list `integer/compare-float-boxed` (and note `from-float-boxed`) in §4.1, or explicitly document the unwrap-and-call as the single sanctioned raw-double crossing.\n\n### P2 concern | §4.3 vs landed frames | `data/nth` hardening diverges from landed `get` reads\n\nThe design mandates \"every read of the 5-slot frame uses `data/nth`\" to defeat guest `(defn get …)` shadowing, but the landed `py`/`php` frames read slots via bare `get` (`(get hs 0)`/`(get hs 3)`/`(get hs 4)` in `frame-depth`, `raise`, `pop-frame`). The Track-B migration of py/js/php onto `yrt.effect` is therefore a **semantic change** (capture-safety), not a rename — the \"bundled == linked\" parity gate must prove the shadowed-`get` case for the migrated preludes, not only for `clj`.\n\n**Correction:** flag the `get`→`data/nth` conversion as a Track-B behavioral migration with its own parity test, rather than implying the landed frames already comply.\n\n### P2 concern | §2.2 invariant 8 / §7.4 | Bundled-`clj` provenance-door trust boundary under-specified\n\nThe design keeps `cell/dsg__new-provenance`/`cell/dsg__provenance` inside bundled **and** linked `clj`, \"never exported\". `state.md`'s door contract is a *privileged mint* + *authenticated reader* whose names guest code must not forge. Linked mode gates the door by content address/admission; **bundled** mode inlines `clj`'s definitions into a tree that may also carry arbitrary guest code, and the mechanism by which the VM distinguishes a trusted `clj`-minted `:cell/new-provenance` from a forged co-bundled call is unspecified.\n\n**Correction:** state the bundled-mode enforcement (e.g. door effects honored only for the emitted `clj` definition addresses, not name-resolvable from guest scope).\n\n## Confirmed properties (passed)\n\n- **CESK integrity (Q1):** sound. `:pure` ops are total/status-returning and never suspend or call guest closures; `ctx-cell` lives in `:heap` (VM state, not continuation state). Policy traps check/return *before* the host op — div-zero is checked pre-call, bit-limit returns a keyword post-call — so `perform`'s `%capture` runs with no host op in flight; Store and Kontinuation are never corrupted, and `%capture` reifies the CESK Kontinuation directly. Moving traps from host throws to guest `perform` changes no Store/Kontinuation state the machine relies on.\n- **Frame mechanics (Q4):** sound. `n` (monotonic frame count, `(+ 1 (frame-depth rest))`) is correctly distinct from `depth` (activation call depth); `(<= (data/nth hs 3) n)` is a valid O(1) structural comparison; `pop-frame` restores both `:handlers` (rest) and `:depth` (slot 4); `restore!` preserves live `:base` while restoring saved `:depth`/`:handlers`, matching landed PHP recursion accounting and Python `:base` rebasing.\n- **`n`-slot vs `:depth`-vs-frame-count (Q4):** sound — mirrors landed `frame-depth`/`pop-frame`.\n\nVM-ENGINEER VERDICT: SOUND WITH CONCERNS — continuation-portability envelope, mixed int×float boxed-comparison export, landed get→data/nth migration, and bundled-provenance-door trust boundary are under-specified; CESK integrity and frame mechanics are sound.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
