, kind)` and lists only those three items; the integer `-boxed` additions (`to-float-boxed`, `true-div-boxed`, `compare-float-boxed`, `from-float-boxed`) are all specified in §7.2, not §4.1. An implementer searching §4.1 will not find them.\ncollab/yang-base/1795207345010-vmengineer-yang-preludes-r8-review-confirm.deepseek-v4-pro.stdout.log:20:§7.2's reconciliation text directs the reader to \"§4.1's integer additions\", but §4.1 defines no integer additions — it is scoped to `data`, `float`, and `kind` only, and every integer `-boxed` export (`to-float-boxed`, `true-div-boxed`, `compare-float-boxed`, `from-float-boxed`) is actually specified in §7.2. **Correction:** either reword line 525 to reference §7.2 (or the `yin.vm.integer` additions wherever they home), or add a fourth numbered item to §4.1 listing the four `integer/*-boxed` exports.\ndocs/design/yang.preludes.md:525:2. **Int × Int:** Delegates directly to `yin.vm.integer` (`add`, `sub`, `neg`, `mul`, `floor-div-mod`, `pow`, `true-div`, `compare`), checking `b == 0` beforehand (performing `:math/div-zero`) and passing every result through `yrt.int/check-limit` before indexing `[q r]` pairs or chaining into further ops. **All host-boundary float carriers are boxed (r8):** `integer/to-float-boxed` for promotion, `integer/true-div-boxed` for division quotients, and boxed `float/neg-pow` for negative exponents — no raw host double enters a guest frame on any Clojure-family numeric path. The frozen native ABI (`integer/to-float`, `true-div`) is unchanged for the legacy track. **Boxed comparison (r8, VM-engineer review):** `integer/compare-float-boxed [x-boxed y-boxed]` (and `integer/from-float-boxed`) are added to the integer host-module exports (listed in §7.2's boxed-path usage) — the landed `compare-float`/`from-float` take raw host doubles and are legacy-only; mixed int×float comparisons on the boxed path never unwrap.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
