ctory-sync-supported?` is true on jolt. `bb probe:jolt-file` also\n110:  over the same namespace. `bb probe:jolt-file` adds the key file's mode and\n120:mechanism remains available for future patches. `bb test:jolt-bootstrap-neg`\n132:`bb test:jolt-cbor-override` is a babashka-only review gate, also run before\n136:host reader branch without evaluating them; it cannot infer macro-generated\n138:`bb test:jolt-cbor-parity` (emit/check) and `dao.stream.cbor-test` on jolt,\n140:acknowledge that review with `bb test:jolt-cbor-override --update \"<who, date>\"`. Document any\n147:bb bootstrap:jolt\n148:bb build:jolt-native\n150:\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\" -Srepro -M:jolt:jolt-yin-repl\n151:bb demo:jolt\n152:bb test:jolt-shell\n153:bb test:jolt-core --only '^yin\\.repl'\n173:The shared reader tests remain active: extra source metadata and accepted\n174:unknown tags/reader conditionals are failures, not accepted divergences.\n\n   A refusal throws `ex-info` whose data carries `:dao.host/refusal`, a\n   class keyword, and `:dao.host/entry`. Every reader conditional names\n   `:cljd` first, because the ClojureDart build also reads `:clj`.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.string :as str]\n    [dao.host.integer :as integer])\n  #?(:cljd (:import [\"dart:typed_data\" ByteData])))\n\n\n(defn- refuse\n  [entry cls detail]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"dao.host refused: \" entry \" \" (name cls) \" (\" detail \")\")\n                  {:dao.host/refusal cls :dao.host/entry entry :detail detail})))\n\n\nsrc/dev/jolt_workload_w.clj:155:    (zero? k) (- 1.0 (Math/pow 0.05 (/ 1.0 n)))\n### 8.1 Multi-host portability (JVM, CLJS/Node, CLJD/Dart, Jolt/Scheme)\n\n- **ClojureDart AOT literal limits:** Consolidate `defquoted` into **`yang.core.defquoted`** (r8 M9 — the dedicated host macro namespace; NOT `yang.core.prelude`, keeping the emission namespace free of macro definitions).\n- **Zero bare integral float literals & zero raw host doubles in guest UAST:** All float operations pass boxed `data/floa